  "coordination_rules": [
    "The control chat does not implement tickets and does not maintain a second status register.",
    "Each ticket runs in its own task chat and produces its own evidence.",
    "A ticket is executable only when its own status is ready and every depends_on ticket is accepted.",
    "After accepted predecessor evidence and its owned commit are present in the shared baseline, the control chat may promote only dependent ticket front matter from draft to ready; it may never mark an execution ticket accepted.",
    "Concurrent implementation requires separate branches or worktrees and non-overlapping owned files.",
    "The graph grants no commit, push, merge, release, or deploy authority; each launch message must carry any additional Git authority explicitly.",
    "After merge or conflict-producing changes, dependent tickets must refresh their baseline before writing.",
    "No chat may infer acceptance from commentary, a branch name, or graph position."
  ],
